4-202.16 The following surfaces need maintenance repair:
1) Gasket on the walk-in freezer door is pulling from bottom and allowing ice to freeze and then melt on the floor. There is minimal ice observed to the right of the walk-in freezer door and some water in-front of the walk-in freezer door. Repair the gasket;
2) Several of the walk-in cooler shelves are observed rusted (see the base shelves of all three shelving units). The bottom three shelves of each shelving unit should be replaced so they are smooth and easily cleanable;
3) there is ice observed on the fan of the walk-in freezer;
4) floor drain covers are missing on the mop sink and beneath the rethermalizer; 
5) caulking at the mop sink is missing and soiled;
6) there is soiled cardboard being used on the frontline steam table to cover holes in service line. Cease use of this soiled cardboard - potential for cross contamination. 
Repair the aforementioned non-food contact surfaces by June 10. This facility has been reminded multiple times to maintain equipment as an effort to maintain safe food practices. Maintaining functioning equipment and keeping surfaces cleanable allows the facility to properly handle food and keep the facility free of pests. Maintain operations and facilities so safe food handling occurs. 


 NonFOOD-CONTACT SURFACES shall be free of unnecessary ledges, projections, and crevices, and designed and constructed to allow easy cleaning and to facilitate maintenance.
